  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A hollow spherical ball of uniform density rolls up a curved surface with an initial velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (as shown in figure). Maximum height with respect to the initial position covered by it will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math><br />(take, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets\\qt0048_10c4103a11a2.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 194px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "75",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0048_10c4103a11a2.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 194px;\" /></p><p>The total kinetic energy of the ball at the bottom of the curve can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>K</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the potential energy acquired by the ball when it attains the maximum height is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Equate equation (1) and (2) and simplify to obtain the required height.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (3) to calculate the required height attained by the ball.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>h</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
